1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,435
Seven outdoor pools, eight hot tubs, and a Roman palace right on the Las Vegas Strip.

2
00:00:06,485 --> 00:00:11,190
This is Caesars Palace, and it is made for a trip for two, or a trip with friends.

3
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:19,063
Twenty restaurants, a spa with forty-eight treatment rooms, and a theater just two minutes away on foot.

4
00:00:19,114 --> 00:00:23,607
Here is how I would plan your stay, and my honest score comes at the end.

5
00:00:23,657 --> 00:00:24,920
Start with the pools.

6
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:31,054
Caesars Palace has seven outdoor pools and eight hot tubs, with cabanas and sun loungers around them.

7
00:00:31,104 --> 00:00:35,374
Expedia highlights a top-rated outdoor pool, with open sky above you.

8
00:00:35,423 --> 00:00:40,365
There is a swim-up bar and a poolside bar, so a cold drink is never far away.

9
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:45,915
The pools are open from nine in the morning to six in the evening, so plan your pool day around it.

10
00:00:45,965 --> 00:00:47,207
Now, dinner.

11
00:00:47,257 --> 00:00:53,655
Caesars Palace has twenty restaurants, twelve bars and lounges, and three coffee shops.

12
00:00:53,705 --> 00:00:58,162
Gordon Ramsay's Hell's Kitchen serves lunch and dinner, and it is open daily.

13
00:00:58,212 --> 00:01:06,442
You will also find Nobu, Pronto by Giada, and Bacchanal Buffet, all open daily, and Nobu takes reservations only.

14
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:11,377
Breakfast is cooked to order, served from seven to eleven in the morning.

15
00:01:11,427 --> 00:01:13,077
Now, where you sleep.

16
00:01:13,127 --> 00:01:18,745
Rooms start around three hundred fifty square feet, and the premium rooms reach about six hundred fifty.

17
00:01:18,796 --> 00:01:22,449
Many rooms have Strip views, and some look onto the fountains.

18
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:25,758
Some rooms are Nobu Hotel rooms, with a different look.

19
00:01:25,807 --> 00:01:30,127
Guests give the Augustus fountain view rooms eight point six out of ten.

20
00:01:30,177 --> 00:01:33,152
And many bathrooms have a big soaking tub.

21
00:01:33,202 --> 00:01:34,606
Then, the fun part.

22
00:01:34,656 --> 00:01:39,567
The Qua spa has forty-eight treatment rooms, including rooms for couples.

23
00:01:39,617 --> 00:01:43,114
It also has a steam room, a sauna, and a hot tub.

24
00:01:43,164 --> 00:01:53,106
The casino covers nearly one hundred twenty-nine thousand square feet, with one hundred eighty-five gaming tables and one thousand three hundred twenty-four slot machines.

25
00:01:53,155 --> 00:01:57,518
There is a sportsbook, and the Colosseum theater is a two-minute walk away.

26
00:01:57,569 --> 00:02:02,414
The Forum Shops are three minutes on foot, and the LINQ Promenade is two.

27
00:02:02,464 --> 00:02:04,208
A few things to know before you go.

28
00:02:04,258 --> 00:02:11,155
There is a resort fee, so check what it covers: the gym, internet, phone calls, and pool access.

29
00:02:11,206 --> 00:02:17,491
At check-in, the hotel asks for a daily deposit, and everything is cashless, so bring a card.

30
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:24,066
Parking costs extra, but you do not need a car, and the airport is only eleven minutes away by road.

31
00:02:24,117 --> 00:02:29,778
Book the spa and Nobu ahead, and remember you must be twenty-one to check in.

32
00:02:29,828 --> 00:02:32,338
So, is Caesars Palace worth it?

33
00:02:32,388 --> 00:02:38,613
On Expedia, guests give it eight point two out of ten, from more than seventeen thousand verified reviews.

34
00:02:38,663 --> 00:02:42,868
Cleanliness scores eight point six, and amenities eight point four.

35
00:02:42,918 --> 00:02:45,418
My honest score is eight out of ten.

36
00:02:45,468 --> 00:02:51,453
It is a great fit for couples and groups who want pools, big dinners, and the Strip at their door.

37
00:02:51,503 --> 00:02:53,650
The link is in the description.
